<title>POLAND: POLISH MINIMUM T-BILL PRICES ALL RISE AT TENDER.</title>
<headline>POLISH MINIMUM T-BILL PRICES ALL RISE AT TENDER.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of all Polish T-bills rose at Monday's primary auction on total demand of 2.863 billion zlotys against the treasury's 1.3 billion zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The finance ministry sold all 1.3 billion zlotys worth of T-bills on offer.  </p>
<p>The treasury will offer 1.4 billion zlotys worth of T-bills</p>
<p>on Monday, May 5. Ministry officials said that the T-bill</p>
<p>tender schedule for May should be available later in the week.</p>
<p>    T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week  52-week</p>
<p>   new min price   96.84    94.87    90.20     ---     82.14</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)  (96.76)  (94.78)  (90.11)    ---    (82.01)</p>
<p>   new max price   97.18    95.00    90.50     ---     82.40</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)  (97.21)  (94.95)  (90.50)    ---    (82.04)</p>
<p>   offer	     200.0    300.0    200.0     ---     600.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded   662.6    703.2    409.4     ---   1,087.5</p>
<p>   bids accepted   200.0    300.4    200.0     ---     600.0</p>
<p>   next auction     ---     400.0    300.0     ---     700.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
